### DATA-LAYOUT-2: bridge ledger default flips to DATA_DIR/data/bridge_deposits.db

Every consumer's unset default is now <data dir>/data/bridge_deposits.db —
matching the Phase-3 fleet layout where BRIDGE_DEPOSITS_DB is set in
blockchain.env on all five hosts (behaviour unchanged while the override
is set). A host that ever loses the variable now resolves the moved
location instead of silently recreating an empty ledger at the top level.
init_db in the monitor and wallet logs a WARNING when its resolved path
is outside DATA_DIR/data. Doc/help examples and the fleet-config-check
probe updated; bridge ledger now backs up as chain_bridge_deposits.db.gz.


### BR-6c: collector classifies sell-lock/settlement release legs

- `bridge_outbound_collect.py` now looks up outbound sends in
  `bridge_sell_locks` and `exchange_settlements` (mirroring the monitor's
  `_RELEASE_SOURCES`, sync comment in place) in addition to
  `eth_withdrawals` — re-runs emit `withdrawal` with the source named in
  `note` instead of `unidentified`. Behaviour on the 16 Oct backfill set
